I'll see you next time.

13
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:28,280
I'll see you next time.

14
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:32,360
Sorry about that.

15
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:33,900
Did we make you wait long?

16
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:35,940
Not at all.

17
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:36,800
I just got here.

18
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:37,540
Thank goodness.

19
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:38,840
I was super worried.

20
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,100
Either way, thanks for being so patient.

21
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:46,300
I've been hearing a lot of rumors involving Sadako everywhere lately.

22
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:49,160
I mean, she did make a big scene the other day.

23
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:51,940
I wonder what kind of girl she really is.

24
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:53,280
I don't know much about her.

25
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:54,200
Oh, yeah.

26
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,760
Didn't we see her hanging out with Kaze Haya before?

27
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:57,620
Oh, yeah.

28
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:58,620
I remember that.

29
00:01:58,740 --> 00:01:59,920
And we were both saying stuff like,

30
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,880
Oh my gosh, are the two of them dating now?

31
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:04,480
There's no way that would ever happen.

32
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:05,820
You think so?

33
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:11,140
If Kaze Haya did actually like her, would it be that weird?

34
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,860
Of course it would!

35
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,380
She'd never even stand a chance!

36
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:20,880
Kaze Haya is a total good guy, so naturally he's gonna be overly nice to her!

37
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:23,640
Besides, if you'd like anyone to beat you, Kurumi!

38
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:25,880
No, that's impossible!

39
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,020
What are you saying?

40
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,700
You two are so close, aren't you?

41
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,340
That's only because we both went to the same middle school.

42
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,900
Jeez, why don't you two just go out already?

43
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:34,760
Not happening.

44
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,780
Even if you don't feel that way, maybe Kaze Haya will eventually fall for you.

45
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,560
This only started recently.

46
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,880
But it seems there's been somewhat of a...

47
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:47,560
mysterious phenomenon happening in the way my classmates interact with me.

48
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:49,880
Hey, it's Sadako!

49
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:53,700
Hey, you, make a goofy face to see if she laughs.

50
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:54,360
What?

51
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:55,900
Oh, you mean like a funny one?

52
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:57,680
Look!

53
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:58,280
Look!

54
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,780
Oh, uh, okay.

55
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:10,780
It didn't work.

56
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:11,920
Mission failed.

57
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:17,560
I'm not sure how to describe it because it's such a new feeling.

58
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:21,080
But I'm just glad people aren't avoiding me anymore.

59
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,140
Oh, you don't know?

60
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:26,620
People are saying that fortune comes to those who make Sadako smile.

61
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:27,780
Fortune?

62
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:31,140
This is the first time anyone's said that about me.

63
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,440
I'm happy for you.

64
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:36,060
Okay, I'll smile for them.

65
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:39,200
Hey, Nakanishi, tell Sadako a joke.

66
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:40,100
Right.

67
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,940
Why'd the hen cross the road to get to the other side?

68
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:43,920
Funny, right?

69
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:49,620
Uh, that one was definitely a fail.

70
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,440
Yeah, in more ways than one.

71
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:54,360
Why does that happen every time you try to smile, Sadako?

72
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:56,040
Morning.

73
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:56,900
Hey.

74
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:57,260
Morning!

75
00:03:58,220 --> 00:04:00,580
Yano, Yoshida, good morning to you both.

76
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:01,840
Look at you.

77
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:06,120
It seems like you've recently become pretty good friends with Hirano and Endo as well.

78
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:06,920
Huh?

79
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,320
F-friend?

80
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,040
Right?

81
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:10,960
All of us are friends now.

82
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:14,480
I didn't actually realize it, but...

83
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:16,320
I-I'm so happy.

84
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:19,640
This is the best moment of my life.

85
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:23,580
Speaking of, it's kind of a pain to keep using your last names.

86
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,180
Can we go off a first name basis?

87
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:26,080
Sure.

88
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:27,760
Just go ahead and call me Eko.

89
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:28,960
And I'm Tomo.

90
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:32,620
All right, then you two can feel free to just call us Chizu and Ayane.

91
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:33,300
Okay.

92
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,240
So, Chizu and Ayane.

93
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:35,820
Got it.

94
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:38,400
Thanks for making sure to include me in there.

95
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:39,240
So...

96
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,600
So smooth.

97
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:41,500
Huh?

98
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,020
What is...

99
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:46,280
That's how everyone gets comfortable calling each other by their first names.

100
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,000
I'm learning a lot today.

101
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,900
No, this is honestly not how it usually goes at all.

102
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:54,940
Normally, you'd go with the flow and start using them as you become closer with people.

103
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,880
I mean, you get it, don't you?

104
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:58,800
Eko.

105
00:04:59,360 --> 00:04:59,800
Tomo.

106
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,000
Chizu.

107
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,060
And Ayane.

108
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:02,680
See?

109
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:04,380
We want you to use first names, too.

110
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:05,000
Huh?

111
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,140
Seriously?

112
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,940
What are you waiting for?

113
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:09,580
Give it a little try.

114
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:16,700
Ayane...

115
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:16,980
Oh!

116
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:17,980
She said it!

117
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,220
Ch-ch-ch-ch-chizu!

118
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,980
Are you gonna be okay?

119
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:24,980
E-e-e-e-e-eko...

120
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:26,940
T-t-tomo...

121
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:27,900
Wow!

122
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:28,920
That's different.

123
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,640
Ah, I like it.

124
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,280
Come on, Sawago.

125
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:34,200
Again, again!

126
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:35,900
You gotta practice!

127
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:42,480
I guess they really liked that.

128
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:51,220
You're too formal with people when you initially meet them anyway.

129
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:55,060
You should try calling girls in class by their first names from now on.

130
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:57,820
Their first names? Isn't that being too friendly?

131
00:05:58,340 --> 00:05:59,760
I don't think it'll be a problem.

132
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:03,040
Guess you're seriously not used to these kind of things, huh?

133
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:07,380
Well, I'm sure it won't happen right away, so just start with your friends.

134
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:12,640
Ah, I think I may have found a good test subject.

135
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,080
Test subject?

136
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:19,280
As an experiment, why don't you try calling him by his first name?

137
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:23,000
What? My justice... No, I can't, Yano!

138
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:23,800
Yano, huh?

139
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:28,500
I mean, uh, Ayane? That's too difficult for me!

140
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:32,560
Come on, how do you think you're supposed to get closer to people if you don't try?

141
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,420
Yano-Chin's a sadist.

142
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:37,260
After all, weren't you going to do your best?

143
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:39,340
Good morning, hey!

144
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,860
Oh, Kasehaya! Sanako said she had something to say to you.

145
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:43,380
Hmm?

146
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:44,700
Go!

147
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:51,560
K-Kasehaya!

148
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,060
That's his last name.

149
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:57,640
Yeah? What?

150
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:03,240
Hi.

151
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:04,560
Hi?

152
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:05,060
Kasehaya!

153
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:05,560
Kasehaya!

154
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:05,900
Kasehaya!

155
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:10,160
It's harder with guys, so that's why I'm saying you should stick to only girls for the time being.

156
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,020
As pushy as always.

157
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,320
Th-that was nerve-wracking!

158
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,940
Right, start with the girls.

159
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:20,940
Okay, I'll do my best.

160
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:24,560
And for the boys, I'll keep doing things the way I have been.

161
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,060
I see.

162
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:27,860
I see.

163
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:30,020
So that was all Yano's idea, then.

164
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,020
Boys.

165
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:35,740
He's always so kind to me, just like Yano and Yoshida are.

166
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:40,300
And he talks to everyone regardless of their gender, but...

167
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:43,080
Since Kuro Numa doesn't usually call out to me like that.

168
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,460
Kasehaya is... a boy.

169
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:48,340
I wonder what she was wanting to say.

170
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:52,640
He's similar to Yano and Yoshida, but also very different.

171
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:54,940
How do I put this?

172
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:56,560
He's just...

173
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:59,900
A boy.

174
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:06,900
Uh, for today's homeroom, we're deciding on the field day committee member.

175
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:10,440
Choosing is a pain, so I've decided the P.E. rep wins.

176
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:11,600
There, that was easy.

177
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:12,600
That's me.

178
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:13,240
Huh?

179
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:17,600
There was no chance to volunteer.

180
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:20,020
So get to work.

181
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:23,000
And if you're wondering who's in charge of the committee, it's me.

182
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:25,580
So if you don't go, I'll spread all of your embarrassment.

183
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:26,740
All right, all right, I know.

184
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:28,160
I'll make sure I'm always there, okay?

185
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:29,540
Listen up.

186
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,640
Every single one of you better take first place.

187
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,640
We don't have enough people here,

188
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,160
so anyone who's athletic will compete in several events.

189
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:39,020
Anybody experienced in a sport must play that sport.

190
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,860
If you don't think you're athletic enough,

191
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:42,320
don't even show up!

192
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:45,160
What a scumbag.

193
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:48,160
And so that leaves us with...

194
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:52,920
Gah!

195
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:56,100
My arms want to move.

196
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,200
My legs are pumped to go.

197
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,520
It's almost go time.

198
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:01,540
My moment is coming.

199
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:03,300
Yes!

200
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:04,880
And let the fire burn in you.

201
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,120
We're gonna win.

202
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:07,860
First place is ours.

203
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:09,880
We're gonna take them all down.

204
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:11,520
These two are exhausting.

205
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:15,100
I have to make sure I don't drag everyone down.

206
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:17,560
Kuro Numa, do you play soccer?

207
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,280
Oh, no, not at all.

208
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:22,060
Is that so?

209
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:24,860
Not surprising since you don't look all that athletic.

210
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:27,320
I'm gonna give field day everything I've got.

211
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:28,760
You don't have to, you know?

212
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:30,740
I'd suggest you take the day off.

213
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:36,280
I have an idea.

214
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:39,140
Why don't we all get a little practice in during our lunch break?

215
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:40,300
Huh, good idea.

216
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:41,620
Let's do it.

217
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,600
Yeah.

218
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,040
I think that would really help.

219
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:47,520
Okay.

220
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,780
Let's give it our all then.

221
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:54,300
I'll do my best.

222
00:09:56,860 --> 00:09:58,600
Practice for field day, huh?

223
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,140
I don't really wanna.

224
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:03,060
But at least having Kazehaya around will make it more interesting.

225
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:05,040
Speaking of Kazehaya,

226
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:07,700
the poor guy was volunteered instantly, wasn't he?

227
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:08,320
Yep.

228
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:27,260
By the way, isn't homeroom our next class coming up?

229
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:28,180
Oh, yeah, you're right.

230
00:10:28,180 --> 00:10:30,920
I wonder if we're gonna decide everyone's field day events.

231
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:32,600
Oh, that reminds me.

232
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,560
Kazehaya's on the field day committee.

233
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:36,280
He's representing class D.

234
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:37,540
Wow, is he really?

235
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,480
Maybe you should become a member of the committee also.

236
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:41,120
What?

237
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:42,840
You think I should?

238
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,720
There's really no reason not to, so why not try it out?

239
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,920
This could end up being how you and Kazehaya get together.

240
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,100
I don't think so.

241
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,920
How many times do I have to tell you that's not gonna happen?

242
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:55,780
Though I wouldn't actually mind becoming a committee member.

243
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:56,660
See?

244
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:57,600
So try.

245
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,700
I can't volunteer myself for the position.

246
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,920
It's too embarrassing.

247
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:02,940
Don't worry.

248
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,720
We can be the ones who recommend you.

249
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:08,600
Your face is so red, Kurumi.

250
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,240
All right, heads up!

251
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,040
Hey, Saniko!

252
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:15,480
Got it!

253
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:27,420
Oopsie-doodles.

254
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:30,180
Yeah, that's what I figured.

255
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:36,720
Hmm, I guess playing an actual match is a little too advanced.

256
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:40,440
Sadako, you'll need to start with the basics of kicking the ball.

257
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:42,660
I'm sorry I'm so incompetent.

258
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,040
It's fine.

259
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:46,360
We know you won't be perfect when you don't have experience.

260
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:49,500
You should really try smiling instead of looking so sad, Sadako.

261
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:52,880
The people on the opposing team might freak out if they see her smile.

262
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:55,600
Or maybe it'll give us enough good fortune to win.

263
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,280
Hey, Chizu!

264
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:02,300
If we don't start heading back soon, then we'll be late for fifth period.

265
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:03,760
Oh, you gotta be kidding.

266
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,360
Is it just me or does lunch break feel shorter?

267
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:10,220
Yikes, and the sports teams use the fields after school, so that's out.

268
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,760
Ugh, this is bad.

269
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:15,120
I'm already weighing everyone down during practice.

270
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:18,500
Come on, Sawako, you can't keep wasting their precious time.

271
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:20,340
I have to train on my own.

272
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:23,320
But I'll need to get a soccer ball.

273
